{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '124,167p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '39,97p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '1,45p' /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '124,167p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '39,97p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '1,45p' /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\"","aggregated_output":"### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\n\nEvidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\nand [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\n\nSales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\nrecognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\nreference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\nsettlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\nand changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\nrestatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\nspecifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\nproperties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\n\nRequired repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\nopening state, event schedules, journal templates and all statement mappings.\nCarry it across annual and interim periods, including a correction and one\nperimeter or currency case. Every supported operation needs its assumptions,\npreconditions, state changes and expected reports; explicit exclusions are\nacceptable. A balanced financing illustration does not specify this package.\n\n### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\n\nEvidence: [proposed demonstrator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:128),\n[ingestion](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:6),\nand [example request](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:234).\n\nThe document proposes a real company and a synthetic company but does not\ninstantiate either as a full disclosure package. There is no named filing\nset with source passages, extracted records, alternative readings, resolved\ncross-references, history constraints and resulting conditional statements.\nThe mathematical example starts after the consequential interpretation work\nhas already been supplied by hand.\n\nRequired repair: add a complete synthetic fixture whose hidden history is known\nand a bounded, named real annual/interim disclosure case. Show representative\nnotes including narrative qualifications, missing terms, a contradiction and\na revised comparative. A worked specification can be written before the\nengine exists; the gap is not simply the absence of production code.\n\n### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\n\nEvidence: [forward equations](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:119),\n[probability mixture](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:170),\n### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\n\nRequirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\nEvidence: [source coverage](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:6)\nand [narrative assertions](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:44).\n\nThe draft requires dispositions for source spans and separates document,\nsemantic and simulation coverage. It does not specify how to establish the\ncomplete disclosure inventory, resolve incorporated cross-references, carry\nqualifications from narrative into the affected figures, or verify that the\ncoverage process itself has not missed a note or table. Generic actor/predicate\nfields are insufficient to determine the executable meaning of exclusions,\nscope qualifications, contingent commitments and qualitative quantifiers.\n\nRequired evidence: one complete filing manifest, source-span disposition and\ncross-reference example; typed narrative records; a mapping from disclosures\nto supported constraints or explicit unresolved obligations. Preserve separate\ncoverage meanings and defined denominators. Do not score parsed pages as\nformalised financial meaning, or turn \"substantially all\" into an invented\nnumeric threshold.\n\n### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\n\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\n\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\n\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\n\nRequirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\nEvidence: [time and views](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:80)\nand [EvidenceView](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:92).\n\nStoring dates and supersession links does not specify which assertion wins a\nquery. The design needs precise rules for incomplete publication timestamps,\nconflicting available filings, selective restatements, changed accounting\nbases and calendars, and different investor-information versus system-version\nqueries. Prospective estimate changes and retrospective corrections are\ndelegated to future packages without a complete transition example.\n\nRequired evidence: a multi-date example with explicit publication, ingestion,\neconomic and reporting times, original and revised amounts, and the exact\nrecords/results returned by each supported view. Show invalid year-to-date\nsubtractions across revisions as well as a valid one. Declare unsupported\ntiming assumptions rather than silently using the latest available row.\n\n# Global Scientific Coding Agent Policy\n\nThis policy is intended for all projects where an agent writes code, runs\nexperiments, interprets numerical results, or helps with scientific documents.\nIt is project-independent. Project-local `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md` files may\nadd stricter rules for a specific repository.\n\n## Context, Tool Output, And Recovery Discipline\n\n- Keep the active question, current stage, checked findings, evidence paths,\n  remaining execution budget, and exact next action in one concise checkpoint.\n  Replace completed-task instructions with the next task; keep detailed history\n  in linked result files instead of expanding the checkpoint indefinitely.\n- Read only the source ranges and structured-result fields needed for the next\n  decision. Normally return at most about 2,000 tokens per tool response and\n  4,000 per combined batch. Per-command budgets add up: bound the outer tool\n  response too. These are context budgets, not limits on scientific rigor.\n- Search for file names or counts first, then inspect selected matching lines.\n  When output is truncated, narrow the query or read another exact range;\n  do not automatically increase the output allowance or repeat a broad dump.\n- Preserve complete command logs on disk and return exit status, key findings,\n  and artifact paths. Do not print entire nested tool results or recursively\n  reproduce old outputs. Parse only the exact saved session and selected fields\n  when investigating an incident; never dump raw session JSONL or instruction\n  payloads into the active research conversation.\n- Use explicit working directories and cross-checkout paths. Save findings\n  after each substantive result and before a large operation. Checkpoint well\n  before the configured compaction threshold; no universal threshold or output\n  setting proves that a model provider can complete compaction.\n- While compaction is unreliable, use fresh research conversations at completed\n  stage boundaries, initialized from the concise checkpoint and governing\n  instructions. Keep incident investigation separate. Resuming or forking a\n  failed conversation can retain its oversized history. Continue authorized\n  work within a healthy stage; this rule creates no new approval gate and does\n  not authorize launching another agent without the applicable authorization.\n- After repeated pre-turn compaction failures, preserve the failed session and\n  recover from the checkpoint. Do not inflate the declared context window,\n  remove applicable instructions, or disable safeguards to force old history\n  through. Tool-output discipline reduces pressure; provider faults require\n  separate diagnosis. Distinguish character counts, active-context token counts,\n  and cumulative billing counts in incident reports.\n\n## Post-Compaction Verification Protocol\n\n- Treat a compaction summary as a memory aid. The user's current directive and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
